    "k-sym-POKÉMON": {
      "decision": "created",
      "narrativeId": "n-pumpfun-card-gacha",
      "reason": "Created n-pumpfun-card-gacha. Three Pokémon coins (pump.fun x2, MeteoraDBC x1; $5.66M of rolling 24h volume at discovery) share the name, but a name alone is not a story. New evidence found today (it was not in this morning's run): posts of 2026-10-19 and 2026-10-20 say Pump.fun put Collector Crypt card gacha packs into its app (CoinGecko's account: $CARDS up 19% following the integration; another post: about $2M of packs opened since launch; e4:0), and a recap post says the launch spawned COLLECTOOOR and pumped the Pokémon coin (e3:1). Looking past the cluster, two COLLECTOOOR contracts and filled.cards (metadata: \"Powered by @Collector_Crypt\") fit the same story. Five coins qualify (two Pokémon, two COLLECTOOOR, FILLED; about $10.6M combined); the third Pokémon (pump.fun, market cap $66.7K) is under the $100K member bar. This morning's rejection of the Pokémon / collectibles group said the metadata was empty or unrelated and no story was found; the story is now found, so the decision changes on new evidence. The independent source is the CoinGecko X account and the app-usage post, not news or an official page, so the narrative is borderline and flagged for the owner."
    },
    "k-fees": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "Resolves this morning's deferral. Only BORLY (\"Trading fees become compute\") still says fees pay for AI compute; ORBIO, the only other coin that did, is a closed member of a retired narrative, LILLY (\"funded by creator fees\") and AMERICA share only the word \"fees\", and Mimi's fees go to charity. The three-coin bar is not met. The new BORLY search (e2:0) returned call-group promotion, a post saying a USDC and Ondo pairing is coming, and a post calling BORLY a bundled scam (not verified); there is no independent source. BORLY stays a candidate."
    },
    "k-future": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "NOX, UDR, AMERICA, NAFF and PYTHIA share only the word \"future\". The NOX search (e2:2) returned call-group promotion and a scam warning."
